Filebeat (The Lightweight Shipper)
Role: Agent installed on application servers to forward logs.

Why Filebeat instead of Logstash directly on servers?

Logstash is heavy (JVM, 500MB+ RAM)

Filebeat is lightweight (Go binary, 20MB RAM)

Filebeat handles backpressure, backoff, and rotation

Filebeat Config Example:

yaml
# filebeat.yml
filebeat.inputs:
- type: filestream  # Modern (better than 'log' input)
  id: leopay-api-logs
  paths:
    - /var/log/leopay/*.log
  fields:
    environment: production
    service: payment-api
  fields_under_root: true

- type: filestream
  id: nginx-access
  paths:
    - /var/log/nginx/access.log

output.logstash:
  hosts: ["logstash.internal:5044"]
  loadbalance: true

# Retry on failure
output.logstash:
  max_retries: 10
  backoff.init: 1s
  backoff.max: 60s

# No data loss during shutdown
shutdown_timeout: 30s
Filebeat Registry (Critical for "No Duplicates"):
Filebeat keeps a registry file that stores the last read position of every log file.

Location: /var/lib/filebeat/registry/filebeat/data.json

If deleted, Filebeat re-reads ALL logs (duplicates or massive backfill!)